# .dev.vars — local Wrangler dev secrets template (Issue #69 / ADR-0015 §9).
#
# This file is the **fallback path** for local development. It exists
# only to document the canonical 3-name secret contract and as a
# template for the file that `pnpm run generate:dev-vars` writes at
# runtime. It is NOT edited by hand.
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Primary path: `pnpm dev`
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `pnpm dev` invokes `scripts/_run-dev.mjs`, a Windows-safe Node wrapper
# that spawns:
#
#   pnpm exec infisical run --env=dev -- pnpm exec vite dev
#
# with `shell: false` (no POSIX shell substitution) so secrets flow
# straight from Infisical into the Vite process. **No `.dev.vars` file
# is read or written** in this path. The CLI auto-resolves the project
# from the committed `.infisical.json` in the repo root.
#
# Operator prerequisite: be logged in via `pnpm exec infisical login`
# once; the CLI caches the access token under `~/.infisical/`.
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Fallback path: `pnpm run generate:dev-vars`
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# When the CLI path is unavailable (offline, token expired, no
# infisical binary on a fresh workstation), the fallback script
# `scripts/generate-dev-vars.mjs` fetches the same set of secrets via
# the documented Infisical API:
#
#   GET /api/v3/secrets/raw?workspaceId={...}&environment=dev&viewSecretValue=true
#
# and writes them to `.dev.vars` with mode `0o600` (atomic via temp +
# rename, with rollback on failure). The set it pulls is **constrained
# to `wrangler.jsonc#secrets.required`** — anything else in the
# Infisical dev env is silently ignored.
#
# Required env for the fallback:
#   INFISICAL_TOKEN  short-lived operator token
# Optional:
#   INFISICAL_API_URL  default https://secrets.rebuildup.dev
# Usage:
#   pnpm run generate:dev-vars           # default env (dev)
#   pnpm run generate:dev-vars -- --env=dev
#   pnpm run generate:dev-vars -- --dry-run    # print plan only
#
# After running, `pnpm dev` (still wrapped through `_run-dev.mjs`)
# will simply pass the secrets in directly — but `wrangler dev` also
# reads `.dev.vars` natively if present, so the fallback exists for
# non-Vite surfaces (e.g. ad-hoc `pnpm exec wrangler dev` during a
# debugging session).
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3-name contract (ADR-0015 §9 staged design)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The Worker runtime expects exactly these three secret names during
# local dev. Production keeps the **legacy 2-name form** (no
# `BETTER_AUTH_SECRETS` yet); the versioned flip is a separate
# human-gated production ticket, governed by
# `[[release-merge-human-gate]]`.
#
#       ┌─────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────┐
#       │ Name                        │ Why                             │
#       ├─────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤
#       │ BETTER_AUTH_SECRET          │ legacy single signing key       │
#       │                             │ (Better Auth 1.5+ accepts this; │
#       │                             │ deprecated once production      │
#       │                             │ flips to the versioned form)    │
#       ├─────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤
#       │ BETTER_AUTH_SECRETS         │ versioned form (Better Auth     │
#       │                             │ 1.5+, format `1:<hex>`);       │
#       │                             │ preferred in dev so dev matches │
#       │                             │ the eventual production form    │
#       ├─────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤
#       │ MY_WEB_2026_CONSUMER_API_KEY│ home-self-consumption API key   │
#       │                             │ (ADR-0011). Local dev: random;  │
#       │                             │ production: hashed in D1 via    │
#       │                             │ `ensure-home-api-key.mjs`       │
#       └─────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────┘
#
# Do NOT edit this file by hand. It is a template that
# `generate-dev-vars` overwrites. The real `.dev.vars` is gitignored
# and must never be committed.

# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET="redacted-by-infisical-fallback"
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRETS="redacted-by-infisical-fallback"
# MY_WEB_2026_CONSUMER_API_KEY="mk_home_redacted-by-infisical-fallback"
